    Bug 2017004 - Centralize messenger window opening and wait for initial document commit. r=darktrojan


    Refactors `toAddressBook`, `toCalendar`, and `toImport` to use a centralized,
    async `toMessengerWindow` helper. This removes the redundant
    `toOpenWindowByType` and duplicates of the session restoration waiting logic.

    Crucially, this fixes a race condition introduced by the shift to
    synchronous about:blank (Bug 543435). Since the initial empty document
    is now created synchronously, `document.readyState` can be `"complete"`
    before the window is actually ready for interaction.

    The updated toMessengerWindow checks for `isUncommittedInitialDocument`.
    If a new window is opened in this state, the function awaits the
    `mail-tabs-session-restored` notification. This ensures the window
    is fully initialized before returning, preventing UI interaction
    errors in both the application and the test suite.

    The patch also updates affected browser tests to handle the transition
    from synchronous to asynchronous tab opening.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D283472

